  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 223 AM CDT Fri Jun 12 2026\n\nDry, cooler and breezy conditions are expected today with\nwesterly winds gusting into the 25 mph range from late morning\nthrough sunset as highs top out in the lower 80s.\n\nA cold front will move across the northern Plains and upper\nmidwest tonight and then move across the local area Saturday\nnight as low pressure lifts northeast from the southern Plains\ntonight to central IL Saturday evening. This will allow for\nscattered thunderstorms to develop, possibly during Saturday\nafternoon and especially into Saturday evening. While the\nhighest potential for severe storms will be near the track of\nthe surface low, across KS and into south/central IL, still\nenough uncertainty that trends will need to be monitored for\npossible severe thunderstorms across the local area, especially\nthe southwest cwa. There are also some timing differences with\nthunderstorms potentially lingering into early Sunday morning\nacross the southeast cwa. The cold front is expected to move\nsouth of the area Sunday morning with dry and cooler temps again\nSunday as highs may only reach the lower/mid 70s.\n\nModels show a weaker upper trough moving across the Great Lakes\nregion in the Tuesday time frame possibly bringing a chance of \nshowers and thunderstorms and then a strong upper trough moving\nacross the region Wednesday/Wednesday night along with a surface\ncold front bringing a better chance for showers and\nthunderstorms. Depending on timing and precip coverage, temps\ncould increase well into the 80s on Wednesday and then cooler \ntemps for Thursday. cms",
